Patchsu patch 13 (optional): collection folders.

Needs only 0001 (applies to plain osu!lazer 8cb6e6e68d + 0001). Also applies together with 0002–0012.

A collection named "Parent/Child" is a sub-collection of "Parent". Nothing else is stored, so vanilla osu! and
collection exports keep seeing ordinary collections with longer names, and removing the patch loses nothing.
Spaces around "/" and empty parts are ignored ("A / B" = "A//B" = "A/B").

Song select, "Group by: Collections":
- Each collection is a thin folder row (30 px, as tall as the Sort / Group dropdowns): folder icon, name, set count.
  Opening one works like a beatmap set: white strip on the left with the chevron (pointing down), and the folder
  shows its sub-folders first, then its own beatmap sets, which open into their collected difficulties only.
- Sub-folders and everything in them are indented 20 px per level. Folder rows don't slide right when closed.
- One chain of folders is open at a time: opening a sub-folder keeps its parents open, closing a folder closes
  everything inside it, opening a folder elsewhere closes the chain. Selecting a beatmap opens its folder chain;
  selecting one in an already open parent keeps the open sub-folders open.
- A beatmap in a collection and in one of its sub-collections is only listed in the outer folder.
- Search / star range / other filters apply inside folders; folders left empty are hidden (so are empty collections,
  like vanilla). "Not in collection" stays a top level folder at the end.
- Right-click a folder: Expand / Collapse, "New sub-collection..." and "Rename..." (a small name box, Enter to
  confirm, "/" nests deeper), "Move to" (Top level or any other folder), "Merge into parent" (sub-folders: their
  beatmaps, sub-collections included, go into the parent collection), "Manage collections...", "Delete" (deletes
  the folder and all its sub-collections, asks first unless it's a single empty collection). Renaming / moving a
  folder carries its sub-collections along.
- Keyboard: left/right from a folder header go to the next / previous beatmap set (into the folder, opening it if
  closed) instead of opening and closing the folder. Group traversal (shift+left/right) skips closed sub-folders and
  steps into an opened folder's sub-folders; shift+enter on a set toggles the set's own folder. Random picks inside
  the open folder, sub-folders included.

Song select, collection filter (the "Collection" dropdown):
- Picking a collection also shows the beatmaps of its sub-collections. If it has sub-collections and "Group by" is None,
  they are folder rows at the top (same folders as above), and the collection's own sets follow them loose.
  Without sub-collections it looks exactly like vanilla.
- The list refreshes as soon as the collection (or a sub-collection) changes. Vanilla only did this in
  "Group by: Collections", so with a filter you had to re-open song select or switch profiles.

Elsewhere:
- Beatmap right-click → Collections (set panel, difficulty panel, results screen collection button): sub-collections
  are nested submenus: "Parent" is still its own toggle (click it), and hovering it opens its sub-collections.
- Manage collections dialog: listed as a tree (sub-collections indented under their parent, which shows only the
  rest of the name), a "+" button per collection adds "New collection" inside it and focuses its name. Renaming a
  parent renames its sub-collections too. The dialog's delete button still deletes only that one collection.

How it works (for later patches):
- New files: Collections/CollectionFolders.cs (path parsing, tree, nested menus, create / rename / move / delete),
  Screens/Select/BeatmapCarouselFilterGrouping.CollectionFolders.cs (builds the folder items; also defines
  CollectionFolderGroupDefinition, equal by path, with a Parent chain), Screens/Select/BeatmapCarousel.CollectionFolders.cs
  (open chain, visibility, indent, spacing), Screens/Select/PanelCollectionFolder.cs.
- Carousel item order is depth first. A folder's GroupItems cover its whole subtree. ExpandedGroup is the deepest open
  folder; its parents count as open.
- Collection filter: FilterControl.CollectionFolders.cs collects the hashes of the collection and its sub-collections and
  sets FilterCriteria.CollectionFolder (the path) when there are sub-collections; the folder builder then starts there,
  with the root's own beatmaps under a null group (always open).
- Small hooks: BeatmapCarouselFilterGrouping.Run (folder modes return early into the folder builder), FilterControl
  (collection subscription condition, CreateCriteria), FilterCriteria.CollectionFolder,
  BeatmapCarousel (spacing, activation, selection, group traversal, setExpandedGroup, set visibility, X offset, pool,
  panel), Carousel.TryFindOwnGroupItem (shift+enter) and ShouldActivateKeyboardSelectionBeforeSetTraversal
  (left/right from a folder header), Panel.ShiftWhenCollapsed, the collection menu builders in
  PanelBeatmapSet / SongSelect / CollectionPopover, DrawableCollectionList(Item), DrawableStatefulMenuItem (a toggle
  with a submenu still toggles on click; the framework only opens the submenu).

diff --git a/osu.Game/Collections/CollectionFolders.cs b/osu.Game/Collections/CollectionFolders.cs
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..c97ffd3bac
--- /dev/null
+++ b/osu.Game/Collections/CollectionFolders.cs
@@ -0,0 +1,304 @@
+// Added by Patchsu
+
+using System;
+using System.Collections.Generic;
+using System.Linq;
+using osu.Framework.Graphics.UserInterface;
+using osu.Game.Database;
+using osu.Game.Graphics.UserInterface;
+
+namespace osu.Game.Collections
+{
+    /// <summary>
+    /// Patchsu patch 13: collection folders.
+    /// A collection named <c>"Parent/Child"</c> is a sub-collection of <c>"Parent"</c>. Nothing else is stored,
+    /// so vanilla osu! (and collection exports) keep seeing ordinary collections with long names.
+    /// </summary>
+    public static class CollectionFolders
+    {
+        public const char SEPARATOR = '/';
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// Splits a collection name into folder segments. Empty segments and spaces around separators are ignored,
+        /// so <c>"A / B"</c>, <c>"A//B"</c> and <c>"A/B"</c> are the same folder.
+        /// </summary>
+        public static string[] Split(string? name)
+        {
+            name ??= string.Empty;
+
+            string[] segments = name.Split(SEPARATOR, StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries | StringSplitOptions.TrimEntries);
+
+            // A name that is only separators / spaces stays a single top level folder.
+            return segments.Length > 0 ? segments : new[] { name.Trim() };
+        }
+
+        public static string Join(IEnumerable<string> segments) => string.Join(SEPARATOR, segments);
+
+        public static string GetPath(string? name) => Join(Split(name));
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// Whether <paramref name="segments"/> is <paramref name="folder"/> itself or anything inside it.
+        /// </summary>
+        public static bool IsSameOrInside(IReadOnlyList<string> segments, IReadOnlyList<string> folder)
+        {
+            if (segments.Count < folder.Count)
+                return false;
+
+            for (int i = 0; i < folder.Count; i++)
+            {
+                if (!string.Equals(segments[i], folder[i], StringComparison.Ordinal))
+                    return false;
+            }
+
+            return true;
+        }
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// Text that is safe to use as one folder name (separators removed).
+        /// </summary>
+        public static string CleanSegment(string? text) => (text ?? string.Empty).Replace(SEPARATOR, ' ').Trim();
+
+        #region Tree
+
+        public class Node
+        {
+            public required string[] Segments { get; init; }
+
+            public string Path => Join(Segments);
+
+            public string Name => Segments[^1];
+
+            public int Depth => Segments.Length - 1;
+
+            public Node? Parent { get; init; }
+
+            public List<Node> Children { get; } = new List<Node>();
+
+            /// <summary>
+            /// Collections whose name is exactly this folder (usually zero or one).
+            /// Zero means the folder only exists because of its sub-collections.
+            /// </summary>
+            public List<BeatmapCollection> Collections { get; } = new List<BeatmapCollection>();
+
+            public IEnumerable<Node> SelfAndDescendants() => Children.SelectMany(c => c.SelfAndDescendants()).Prepend(this);
+        }
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// Builds the folder tree. Order follows the incoming collection order (osu! sorts collections by name realm side).
+        /// </summary>
+        public static List<Node> BuildTree(IEnumerable<BeatmapCollection> collections)
+        {
+            var roots = new List<Node>();
+            var byPath = new Dictionary<string, Node>(StringComparer.Ordinal);
+
+            foreach (var collection in collections)
+            {
+                string[] segments = Split(collection.Name);
+                Node? parent = null;
+
+                for (int depth = 0; depth < segments.Length; depth++)
+                {
+                    string[] nodeSegments = segments[..(depth + 1)];
+                    string path = Join(nodeSegments);
+
+                    if (!byPath.TryGetValue(path, out var node))
+                    {
+                        byPath[path] = node = new Node { Segments = nodeSegments, Parent = parent };
+                        (parent?.Children ?? roots).Add(node);
+                    }
+
+                    parent = node;
+                }
+
+                parent!.Collections.Add(collection);
+            }
+
+            return roots;
+        }
+
+        public static IEnumerable<Node> Flatten(IEnumerable<Node> roots) => roots.SelectMany(r => r.SelfAndDescendants());
+
+        #endregion
+
+        #region Menus
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// Nests collection menu items by folder. A folder with sub-collections is its own collection's toggle (click
+        /// toggles it) with a submenu holding its sub-collections.
+        /// </summary>
+        /// <param name="collections">All collections, in display order.</param>
+        /// <param name="createItem">Creates the toggle for one collection. Its text is replaced by the folder name.</param>
+        public static List<OsuMenuItem> CreateMenuItems(IEnumerable<BeatmapCollection> collections, Func<BeatmapCollection, OsuMenuItem> createItem)
+            => BuildTree(collections).SelectMany(n => createMenuItems(n, createItem)).ToList();
+
+        private static IEnumerable<OsuMenuItem> createMenuItems(Node node, Func<BeatmapCollection, OsuMenuItem> createItem)
+        {
+            var own = node.Collections.Select(c =>
+            {
+                var item = createItem(c);
+                item.Text.Value = node.Name;
+                return item;
+            }).ToList();
+
+            if (node.Children.Count == 0)
+                return own;
+
+            var children = node.Children.SelectMany(c => createMenuItems(c, createItem)).Cast<MenuItem>().ToArray();
+
+            // A folder without a collection of its own ("A/B" exists, "A" doesn't) only opens the submenu.
+            if (own.Count == 0)
+                return new[] { new OsuMenuItem(node.Name, MenuItemType.Standard) { Items = children } };
+
+            own[0].Items = children;
+            return own;
+        }
+
+        #endregion
+
+        #region Editing
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// Creates an empty collection inside <paramref name="parent"/> (or at the top level).
+        /// </summary>
+        /// <returns>The new collection's name.</returns>
+        public static string CreateCollection(RealmAccess realm, IReadOnlyList<string>? parent, string name)
+        {
+            // separators in the name nest it deeper.
+            string[] relative = name.Split(SEPARATOR, StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries | StringSplitOptions.TrimEntries);
+
+            if (relative.Length == 0)
+                relative = new[] { "New collection" };
+
+            string fullName = Join((parent ?? Array.Empty<string>()).Concat(relative));
+
+            realm.Write(r =>
+            {
+                var existing = r.All<BeatmapCollection>().AsEnumerable().Select(c => GetPath(c.Name)).ToHashSet(StringComparer.Ordinal);
+
+                string candidate = fullName;
+
+                for (int i = 2; existing.Contains(candidate); i++)
+                    candidate = $"{fullName} ({i})";
+
+                fullName = candidate;
+                r.Add(new BeatmapCollection(fullName));
+            });
+
+            return fullName;
+        }
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// Moves a folder, with everything inside it, to a new path.
+        /// </summary>
+        /// <returns>The number of collections renamed.</returns>
+        public static int MoveFolder(RealmAccess realm, IReadOnlyList<string> folder, IReadOnlyList<string> newPath)
+        {
+            if (newPath.Count == 0 || IsSameOrInside(newPath, folder))
+                return 0;
+
+            return realm.Write(r =>
+            {
+                int count = 0;
+
+                foreach (var collection in r.All<BeatmapCollection>().ToList())
+                {
+                    string[] segments = Split(collection.Name);
+
+                    if (!IsSameOrInside(segments, folder))
+                        continue;
+
+                    collection.Name = Join(newPath.Concat(segments.Skip(folder.Count)));
+                    collection.LastModified = DateTimeOffset.UtcNow;
+                    count++;
+                }
+
+                return count;
+            });
+        }
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// Renames a folder in place. <paramref name="newName"/> may contain separators to nest it deeper.
+        /// </summary>
+        public static int RenameFolder(RealmAccess realm, IReadOnlyList<string> folder, string newName)
+        {
+            string[] relative = newName.Split(SEPARATOR, StringSplitOptions.RemoveEmptyEntries | StringSplitOptions.TrimEntries);
+
+            if (relative.Length == 0)
+                return 0;
+
+            return MoveFolder(realm, folder, folder.Take(folder.Count - 1).Concat(relative).ToArray());
+        }
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// Moves a folder into <paramref name="newParent"/>, or to the top level when it is empty.
+        /// </summary>
+        public static int MoveFolderInto(RealmAccess realm, IReadOnlyList<string> folder, IReadOnlyList<string> newParent)
+            => MoveFolder(realm, folder, newParent.Append(folder[^1]).ToArray());
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// Moves the beatmaps of a folder and all its sub-collections into the parent collection (created if the parent
+        /// folder only exists through its sub-collections), then removes the folder's collections.
+        /// </summary>
+        /// <returns>The number of collections merged.</returns>
+        public static int MergeIntoParent(RealmAccess realm, IReadOnlyList<string> folder)
+        {
+            if (folder.Count < 2)
+                return 0;
+
+            string parentPath = Join(folder.Take(folder.Count - 1));
+
+            return realm.Write(r =>
+            {
+                var all = r.All<BeatmapCollection>().AsEnumerable().ToList();
+                var inside = all.Where(c => IsSameOrInside(Split(c.Name), folder)).ToList();
+
+                if (inside.Count == 0)
+                    return 0;
+
+                var parent = all.FirstOrDefault(c => GetPath(c.Name) == parentPath);
+
+                if (parent == null)
+                    r.Add(parent = new BeatmapCollection(parentPath));
+
+                var known = parent.BeatmapMD5Hashes.ToHashSet();
+
+                foreach (string hash in inside.SelectMany(c => c.BeatmapMD5Hashes))
+                {
+                    if (known.Add(hash))
+                        parent.BeatmapMD5Hashes.Add(hash);
+                }
+
+                parent.LastModified = DateTimeOffset.UtcNow;
+
+                foreach (var c in inside)
+                    r.Remove(c);
+
+                return inside.Count;
+            });
+        }
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// Deletes a folder and everything inside it.
+        /// </summary>
+        public static int DeleteFolder(RealmAccess realm, IReadOnlyList<string> folder) => realm.Write(r =>
+        {
+            var toDelete = r.All<BeatmapCollection>().AsEnumerable().Where(c => IsSameOrInside(Split(c.Name), folder)).ToList();
+
+            foreach (var c in toDelete)
+                r.Remove(c);
+
+            return toDelete.Count;
+        });
+
+        /// <summary>
+        /// Counts the collections in a folder (including the folder's own) and the beatmaps they hold.
+        /// </summary>
+        public static (int collections, int beatmaps) CountFolder(RealmAccess realm, IReadOnlyList<string> folder) => realm.Run(r =>
+        {
+            var inside = r.All<BeatmapCollection>().AsEnumerable().Where(c => IsSameOrInside(Split(c.Name), folder)).ToList();
+            return (inside.Count, inside.SelectMany(c => c.BeatmapMD5Hashes).Distinct().Count());
+        });
+
+        #endregion
+    }
+}
